Design: AppController.submission_context_for(voice) is the ONE gate — it builds
the context through core.synthesis_context.context_for, which validates
language/speaker/clone against the capability table, and returns None with the
capability table's own actionable message in errorText; a refusal therefore
never queues a job, starts an engine, or registers a listener. The request then
carries that frozen object (voice/temperature/speed/silence_p all read from it),
so nothing re-derives engine identity at render time. Generation settings are
recorded only for controls the profile declares (Qwen CustomVoice/Base record
temperature=None because the 0.6B host ignores it), so a fingerprint never
varies with a setting that cannot change the audio. Language is profile-scoped
and persisted (Settings.synthesis_language, clamped on read); switching drops a
code the incoming profile cannot serve, which keeps memory and the settings file
in agreement, and VieNeu's unset language stays "" because its SDK takes no
language argument at all (Qwen's unset default resolves to "auto"). VieNeu
voices always stay SDK registry names while a Qwen clone row resolves to a
clone id, so the capability table — not the UI — produces the refusal for an
unknown speaker, a fixed speaker offered to Base, or a missing clone. The
audition cache is now auditions/<profile>/<voice>_<language>_<speed>.wav: a
preview rendered by one engine can never be replayed for another (AC9). Qwen
submissions now assemble their own owner: _build_qwen_engine reads only the
verified install locations (no Hub, no download, no load on the GUI thread),
refuses with an actionable reason while the model/runtime is missing or the
device resolve is still in flight (re-kicking the resolve instead of guessing),
and hands the worker an EngineProviders set holding exactly one provider, with
None keeping the worker's single-engine VieNeu default. The Paragraph queue
takes ONE snapshot per run and stamps every pending entry (an entry that joins
mid-run snapshots for itself), so a later settings change can never rewrite
queued work; a refused combination leaves the queue untouched and reports the
app's reason (falling back to its own when a bare fake app has none).
